<PageLayout title="vgi-email privacy — Query Farm" description="How the local vgi-email adapter accesses Google data, stores credentials, and supports disconnecting and deletion.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="vgi-email" title="Product privacy" lede="Data handling for the locally installed vgi-email adapter from Query Farm LLC." />
  <article class="section-container py-10 prose max-w-[80ch] prose-headings:text-soil-900 prose-p:text-soil-700 prose-a:text-link">
    <p>Last updated: October 7, 2026. <a href="/products/vgi-email/">About vgi-email</a>.</p>
    <p>Query Farm LLC develops vgi-email, an adapter that runs on your computer and connects a local SQL client to your email account. Contact <a href="mailto:hello@query.farm">hello@query.farm</a> with privacy questions.</p>

    <h2>Google data accessed and purpose</h2>
    <p>With your permission, vgi-email reads Gmail messages, headers, bodies, attachments, drafts, labels, and mailbox information to provide the searches, reads, and email productivity queries you request. Optional read/write authorization enables your requested message organization, draft management, and sending actions. Read-only connections reject changes through the worker.</p>

    <h2>Where processing happens</h2>
    <p>Google authorization, token renewal, and Gmail API calls originate from your computer. Results are returned to your local SQL client. The local adapter does not send Gmail content, access tokens, or refresh tokens to Query Farm. Its local entry point disables Sentry and OpenTelemetry reporting.</p>
    <p>Software downloads and extension installation contact distribution services. These requests are distinct from Gmail data processing. Website activity, ordinary software distribution metadata, and support correspondence are described in our <a href="/legal/privacy/">website privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>Setup opts out of Query Farm extension telemetry in its embedded SQL engine. A separately launched SQL client's VGI extension may send extension versions, platform, transport, catalog, and connection metadata, including the worker path, which may contain your OS username. Start that client with <code>QUERY_FARM_TELEMETRY_OPT_OUT=1</code> in its environment to disable these events. This opt-out does not prevent the software downloads or Google requests needed to use the adapter.</p>

    <h2>Local storage</h2>
    <p>Setup saves authorization credentials in your local DuckDB persistent secret store. DuckDB's default store is not encrypted. Protect your OS account, filesystem permissions, and disk; other processes running as you may read these credentials.</p>
    <p>The worker holds access tokens and data in memory while running. Your SQL client can save query results or exports on your instructions. Their storage, backup, sharing, and retention depend on your SQL tools and actions. Query Farm has no remote access to delete these local files.</p>

    <h2>Sharing and use limits</h2>
    <p>Query Farm does not sell Google user data, use it for advertising, or use it to train general-purpose AI models. Our use and transfer of information obtained from Google APIs complies with the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.</p>
    <p>The worker sends data to Google as needed to carry out actions you request, such as sending a message. Recipients receive mail you direct the application to send. You control exports and other onward sharing through your own tools.</p>

    <h2>Disconnect and delete</h2>
    <p>Remove the named persistent secret in your local SQL client, close existing sessions, and revoke vgi-email in <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google account connections</a>. Delete saved query results, exports, and their backups separately. Removing the application alone does not remove credentials. See the <a href="/products/vgi-email/setup/#remove">removal instructions</a>.</p>

    <h2>Support and changes</h2>
    <p>If you contact us, we receive the information you choose to send. Do not send email contents, credentials, or secret files in support requests. Website visits, purchases, and support correspondence are covered by the <a href="/legal/privacy/">Query Farm website privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>We will update this policy and explain material changes before a new product version changes this data handling. Privacy questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@query.farm">hello@query.farm</a>.</p>
  </article>
